asks you completed on Friday, 2026-09-26:\\n\\n1. **Meta Order & Revenue Tracking Issue (Maintenance):**\\n   Resolved an issue where Meta dashboard wasn\'t reflecting revenues for some purchases.\\n\\n2. **Tag Update for Meta (Maintenance):**\\n   Updated the Meta tag for order confirmation (LC-Shop-AD(Meta)-OrderConfirmation-WL-SDSME_8471933442900811).\\n\\n3. **New Firework Tag for ZP6_TR-Turkey WebSDK (New Request):**\\n   Implemented a new Firework tag (LC-AEM-AD(Firework)-CM-ALL-WL-SDSME_fw53-18f99c7061c1) for the Turkey WebSDK.\\n\\n4. **New Firework Tag for ZS_Hybris_TR-Turkey Shop Section (New Request):**\\n   Added a new Firework tag (LC-Shop-AD(Firework)-CM-ALL-WL-SDSME_fw53-18f99c7061c1) for the Turkey Shop Section.\\n\\nThese tasks involved resolving a Meta tracking issue, updating a Meta tag, and implementing two new Firework tags for Turkey-related WebSDKs.\"}]', '2026-09-28 11:11:32', '2026-09-28 11:12:57'),
('21', '1', '612', 'Please check the script if my function t...', '[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Please check the script if my function trackPageVisit() is correct\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"Your `trackPageVisit()` function is close, but it has a few important issues that will affect data accuracy in Pinterest:\\n\\n1. **`event_id` is reused for both events on the PDP**  \\n   You call `trackPageVisit(\'pagevisit\')` and `trackPageVisit(\'viewcontent\')`, but both use the same `eventId`. Pinterest uses `event_id` for deduplication. Different events must have different IDs.  \\n   \\u2192 Generate a new `event_id` inside `trackPageVisit()`.\\n\\n2. **`eventId` is based on seconds**  \\n   `Math.floor(Date.now() \\/ 1000)` will repeat if two events happen in the same second. Use `Date.now()` plus a random suffix.\\n\\n3. **`value` and `product_price` are often strings, not numbers**  \\n   `product.model_price` looks like `\\\"0,4799\\\"`. Pinterest expects numeric values. Sending `\\\"Unknown\\\"` as a price is invalid. Normalize the price to a number or omit it.\\n\\n4. **`digitalData.product` may be undefined**  \\n   If any page lacks `digitalData.product`, the function will throw. Add a guard.\\n\\n5. **Potential duplicate `pagevisit` event**  \\n   Your base snippet already has `pintrk(\'page\');`, which itself tracks a page visit. Then you manually fire `trackPageVisit(\'pagevisit\')` on PDPs. That will create duplicate page-visit events. You probably only need `viewcontent` on the PDP, or remove `pintrk(\'page\')` if you want full control. That depends on your tagging plan.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommended corrected function\\n\\n```javascript\\nfunction getEventId() {\\n  return \'evt_\' + Date.now() + \'_\' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10);\\n}\\n\\nfunction normalizePrice(value) {\\n  if (typeof value === \'number\' && Number.isFinite(value)) return value;\\n  if (typeof value !== \'string\') return undefined;\\n\\n  let cleaned = value.trim();\\n\\n  if (cleaned.includes(\',\')) {\\n    const parts = cleaned.split(\',\');\\n    if (parts.length === 2) {\\n      \\/\\/ \\\"4,799\\\" \\u2192 4799\\n      \\/\\/ \\\"0,4799\\\" \\u2192 0.4799\\n      cleaned = parts[1].length === 3 ? parts.join(\'\') : parts.join(\'.\');\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  const num = Number(cleaned);\\n  return Number.isNaN(num) ? undefined : num;\\n}\\n\\nfunction trackPageVisit(eventName) {\\n  \\/\\/ Always send an event, but don\'t crash if product data is missing\\n  if (!digitalData || !digitalData.product) {\\n    pintrk(\'track\', eventName, {\\n      event_id: getEventId()\\n    });\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  const product = digitalData.product;\\n  const price = normalizePrice(product.model_price || product.list_price);\\n\\n  const lineItem = {\\n    product_name: product.displayName,\\n    product_id: product.model_code,\\n    product_category: product.pvi_type_name,\\n    product_variant: product.pvi_subtype_name\\n  };\\n\\n  if (price !== undefined) {\\n    lineItem.product_price = price;\\n  }\\n\\n  pintrk(\'track\', eventName, {\\n    event_id: getEventId(),\\n    ...(price !== undefined ? { value: price } : {}),\\n    line_items: [lineItem]\\n  });\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThen on the PDP, you could simplify:\\n\\n```javascript\\ncase \'flagship pdp\':\\ncase \'product detail\':\\n  trackPageVisit(\'viewcontent\');\\n  break;\\n```\\n\\nIf you really need a manual `pagevisit` event too, you can call both, but the unique `event_id` fix will keep them separate.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## One more thing\\n\\nYour `product` data may contain multiple products in one string:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"model_code\\\": \\\"SM-S938BZSOMEA,SM-S937BZSOMEA\\\",\\n\\\"displayName\\\": \\\"Galaxy S25 Ultra;Galaxy S25 Edge\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThe current `line_items` sends them as one combined item, which is probably not correct. If that page really represents multiple products, split them into separate line items. But if that data is a data-layer quirk, you may want to use only the first value or a specific product code.\\n\\nOverall: your structure is good, but make the `event_id` unique per event, normalize prices, and protect against missing product data.\",\"reasoning_content\":null}]', '2026-09-28 15:26:32', '2026-09-28 15:26:32');
